From e9488c6286ec9dab3094aa2fb22ef3ce5e452f45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy Lyons <guylyons2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:38:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] macos-arm64: RT cost control: coherent ray blocks, GPU
 budget, 64-unit AO radius

Enclosed scenes (tunnels, corridors) cost up to 3x the open-air trace on the
software tracer because every divergent ray walks to a nearby hit. AO
directions are now shared across 2x2 pixel blocks (rt_coherent, ~25% cheaper,
the temporal sequence still varies per frame), the default AO radius is 64
units, and a budget controller (rt_budget, 7 ms) drops to one AO ray per pixel
while the tracer's smoothed GPU time is over budget. The canal tunnel goes from
15 ms to 6 ms per traced frame.
---
